mixin () {
  /// Static Markdown documentation of the backend's public API.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Wave Maker Backend API\n\n## Purpose\n\nThe backend stores a single, app-session-wide high score for the Wave Maker\nendless runner. It is intentionally minimal: the game runs entirely in the\nbrowser, and the canister only records the best distance reached during the\ncurrent session so the game-over screen can show it.\n\n## Authentication and authorization\n\nNo method requires a signed-in caller. Both `getSessionHighScore` and\n`submitRun` are callable by anonymous and signed-in principals alike, and the\nhigh score is shared across every caller of the canister — it is not tied to a\nuser identity. There is no owner or admin restriction on these methods.\n\nThe app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at\n`/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding\nthe user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app\nprincipal against that origin (for example\n`icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the\nuser's full authority in this app until it expires. Because this backend does\nnot gate on identity, that authority grants no additional access here.\n\n## Methods\n\n### `getSessionHighScore() : async nat` (query)\n\nReturns the current session high score as a `nat` distance in game units.\nReturns `0` before any run has been recorded. This is a query call: it reads\nstate without modifying it and is safe to poll.\n\n### `submitRun(distance : nat) : async nat`\n\nRecords a finished run's `distance` (in game units) and returns the resulting\nsession high score. The stored high score only ever increases: submitting a\ndistance lower than the current high score leaves it unchanged, and the\nreturned value is always the maximum of the previous high score and the\nsubmitted distance.\n\n## Units and encoding\n\n- Distances are unsigned integers (`nat`) in game units, matching the\n  distance counter shown in the game.\n- There are no timestamps, blobs, or optional values in this API.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n- `getSessionHighScore` is a query and may be polled freely; it never mutates\n  state.\n- The high score persists in canister stable state across upgrades, but it is\n  a single shared session value rather than a per-user or per-run history.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n`submitRun` is idempotent with respect to the high score: re-submitting the\nsame distance, or any distance not exceeding the current high score, produces\nthe same stored value and the same return value. Retrying a `submitRun` call\nthat may have succeeded is therefore safe and cannot inflate the score.\n\n## Errors and gotchas\n\n- Neither method traps for ordinary input; any `nat` distance is accepted.\n- The high score is global to the canister session, so concurrent players\n  share one value. This is intentional for the single-player session model.\n- There is no endpoint to reset the high score.\n";
  };
};
